# Spectra Backend

Package root: `com.dertz.spectra`. Context path `/api`.

## Security & tenancy

- Stateless JWT; claims drive `TenantContext` (`tenantId`, `branchId`, `userId`, `role`)
- Validate `X-Branch-Id` against user’s allowed branches (except platform-only routes)
- Every tenant entity: `tenant_id` + Hibernate `@TenantId` / filters; never query without tenant scope
- Clear `TenantContext` in finally after seed/async work

## Persistence

- Schema **only** via Flyway under `backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/`
- Next migration = max `V{n}` + 1; additive, reversible-friendly; indexes on `(tenant_id, …)`
- Services own transactions (`@Transactional`); controllers stay thin
- FEFO is shared — vaccines, multi-item consumption, staff POS, audit write-offs reuse one allocate path (unified warehouse target; do not add a second stock engine)

## API

- Envelope: `ApiResponse` `{ success, data, message, errorCode }`
- Role gates on controllers must match `.cursor/rules` RBAC (inventory manager may run ops menus; cannot create `NGO_ADMIN` / `PLATFORM_ADMIN`)
- Prefer existing services (`InventoryService`, `DogService`, `PayrollService`, `OpsDomainService`, …) over new god-classes

## Example

```java
// ❌ BAD — adjust qty outside FEFO / audit review
batch.setQtyOnHand(physical);

 // ✅ GOOD — flag audit, then review → APPROVED_WRITE_OFF applies delta via service
inventoryService.flagAudit(request);
inventoryService.reviewAudit(id, writeOff);
```
